+# Applying and building RNSBox
+
+RNSBox ships as a `git format-patch` series on top of the upstream Sipeed board
+support package. You apply the series onto a pristine upstream checkout and run
+the RNSBox build driver.
+
+## 1. Get the upstream base
+
+```
+git clone https://github.com/sipeed/LicheeRV-Nano-Build.git
+cd LicheeRV-Nano-Build
+git checkout d4003f15b35d43ad4842f427050ab2bba0114fa5
+```
+
+The series was generated against exactly this commit.
+
+## 2. Apply the RNSBox patch series
+
+```
+git am /path/to/rnsbox-patches/*.patch
+```
+
+If you would rather not create commits, `git apply` also works:
+
+```
+git apply /path/to/rnsbox-patches/*.patch
+```
+
+## 3. Build
+
+RNSBox uses the upstream CVITEK build flow with a single driver that selects
+the image variant:
+
+```
+./build-rnsbox.sh dvd     # full image + read-only clients disc (~2.8 GB)
+./build-rnsbox.sh lite    # NCM-only image, no clients disc (~217 MB)
+```
+
+Notes:
+
+- The first build compiles a **Rust host toolchain from source** (required for
+  `python-cryptography` on riscv64-musl, which in turn is required by
+  Reticulum). Expect this to take a while on the first run only.
+- The `dvd` variant expects the Reticulum client binaries under `dl/clients/`.
+  Run `./fetch-clients.sh` first and review `build/clients-stick/` — see the
+  follow-up note in [README.RNSBox.md](README.RNSBox.md). The `lite` variant
+  needs none of this.
+- Output images land under `install/soc_sg2002_licheervnano_sd/images/`,
+  suffixed `-dvd` / `-lite`.
+
+## 4. Flash
+
+```
+sudo dd if=install/soc_sg2002_licheervnano_sd/images/<image>.img \
+        of=/dev/sdX bs=4M conv=fsync status=progress
+```
+
+Make sure `/usr/sbin` is on `PATH` so genimage's `mkfs.fat` resolves. The DVD
+image needs a microSD comfortably larger than the ~3.3 GB DVD image (e.g. 8 GB); the rootfs auto-grows to fill the card
+on first boot.
+
+Then plug the board into a host over USB-C and browse to `http://10.42.0.1/`
+(admin / admin).
